{
  "_comment": [
    "Golden corpus for the non-CVE rules: labelled inputs with the findings each must",
    "produce. Consumed by corpus_test.go NOW — a corpus with no checker is a dead file,",
    "which is the failure this project warns against — and week 8's make corpus-check is to",
    "drive these same cases end to end through a real scan (docs/execution-plan.md 6.2).",
    "",
    "Each case is one service observation and the rule names it must and must not raise.",
    "'raises' is exact: a rule not listed must NOT fire, because a false finding costs more",
    "than a missed one (the write-detection-rule skill)."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "expired-self-signed-cert",
      "service": {
        "port": 443, "protocol": "tcp", "service": "http",
        "tls": {"version": "TLSv1.2", "cipher_suite": "TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256", "chain_length": 1,
          "chain": [{"subject": "CN=old", "issuer": "CN=old", "not_before": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z", "not_after": "2025-01-01T00:00:00Z", "self_signed": true, "public_key_algorithm": "RSA", "key_bits": 2048}]}
      },
      "environment": "",
      "raises": ["tls-certificate-expired", "tls-self-signed-non-dev"]
    },
    {
      "name": "self-signed-on-dev-is-exempt",
      "service": {
        "port": 443, "protocol": "tcp", "service": "http",
        "tls": {"version": "TLSv1.3", "cipher_suite": "TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256", "chain_length": 1,
          "chain": [{"subject": "CN=dev", "issuer": "CN=dev", "not_before": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z", "not_after": "2027-01-01T00:00:00Z", "self_signed": true, "public_key_algorithm": "RSA", "key_bits": 2048}]}
      },
      "environment": "dev",
      "raises": []
    },
    {
